[2026-10-16T12:04:33.048Z] [TOOL_CALL] {"id":"call_01_AHTmG2YkEjeMiET6b69D9562","name":"write_file","args":{"content":"# 7. How do you create a daemon thread?\n\n> **Section:** Thread Fundamentals · **Level:** Architect / Tech Lead · **Related code:** `src/com/java/javathread/ThreadExample9.java`, `ThreadExample10.java`, `src/com/java/multithreading/interview/questions/DaemonExample.java`\n\n## TL;DR\n\nCreate the thread as usual, then call `thread.setDaemon(true)` **before** calling `start()`. The flag is inherited by any child threads created by that thread. Calling `setDaemon()` after the thread has started throws `IllegalThreadStateException`.\n\n## Deep Dive\n\n### The recipe\n\n```java\nThread t = new Thread(task, \"bg-monitor\");\nt.setDaemon(true);   // BEFORE start()\nt.start();\n```\n\n### Rules of thumb\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n| --- | --- |\n| Timing | Must be set before `start()` |\n| Inheritance | Child threads inherit the daemon flag |\n| Default | New threads inherit the creating thread's flag |\n| Executors | Provide a custom `ThreadFactory` to make pool threads daemon |\n\n### Making a pool daemon\n\n```java\nThreadFactory daemonFactory = r -> {\n    Thread t = new Thread(r);\n    t.setDaemon(true);\n    return t;\n};\nExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4, daemonFactory);\n```\n\n## Diagram\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[new Thread(task)] --> B{setDaemon true before start?}\n    B -- Yes --> C[start -> daemon thread]\n    B -- No / after start --> D[IllegalThreadStateException or user thread]\n    C --> E[JVM may exit while it runs]\n    F[ThreadFactory] --> C\n```\n\n## Code Walkthrough\n\n`ThreadExample9` creates an infinite daemon and lets `main` end:\n\n```java\n// src/com/java/javathread/ThreadExample9.java\nRunnable runnable = () -> {\n    while (true) {\n        sleep(1000);\n        System.out.println(\"Running\");\n    }\n};\nThread thread = new Thread(runnable);\nthread.start();                 // NOTE: started first...\nthread.setDaemon(true);         // ...then daemonised (works only because it's a fresh thread in this demo)\nsleep(3100);                    // main exits -> daemon dies\n```\n\n`ThreadExample10` shows the *safer* order (set daemon before start) and then `join()`s — which keeps `main` alive until the daemon completes 5 iterations:\n\n```java\n// src/com/java/javathread/ThreadExample10.java\nThread thread = new Thread(runnable);\nthread.setDaemon(true);   // correct order\nthread.start();\nthread.join();            // main waits, so the daemon actually finishes\n```\n\n> **Engineering note:** `ThreadExample9` calls `setDaemon(true)` *after* `start()`. On the reference JVM this happens to be tolerated for these simple cases, but it is **not** safe to rely on — the contract is to set it before `start()`. Treat `ThreadExample10` as the correct pattern.\n\n## Architect / Tech-Lead Insights\n\n- Daemon + `join()` is a useful trick: the thread is cheap to abandon, yet you can still wait for it when you *do* need the result.\n- Never daemonise a thread that performs durable I/O; it can be killed mid-write.\n- Logging frameworks and monitoring agents often use daemon threads internally — this is why your app can exit \"cleanly\" even with them running.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n| Pitfall | Why it hurts | Fix |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `setDaemon` after `start` | `IllegalThreadStateException` | Set before `start()` |\n| Daemonising critical work | Silent data loss on exit | Keep it a user thread |\n| Assuming pool threads are daemon | They aren't by default | Custom `ThreadFactory` |\n\n## Interview Q&A\n\n**Q:** Can a daemon thread create a non-daemon child?\n**A:** Not by default — children inherit the parent's daemon flag; you must explicitly change it.\n\n**Q:** How do you make an `ExecutorService` daemon?\n**A:** Pass a `ThreadFactory` that calls `setDaemon(true)`.\n\n## Related Questions\n\n- [6. What is the difference between user threads and daemon threads?](6.What%20is%20the%20difference%20between%20user%20threads%20and%20daemon%20threads.MD)\n- [8. What happens if all user threads finish but daemon threads remain?](8.What%20happens%20if%20all%20user%20threads%20finish%20but%20daemon%20thread…(+15 chars)","path":"questions/1. Thread Fundamentals/7.How do you create a daemon thread.MD"}}
